      "output": "`TESTPLAN.md` has been written to `/Users/esanmohammad/prototyping/Space-company/TESTPLAN.md`.\n\nHere's a summary of what was produced:\n\n---\n\n## What's in TESTPLAN.md\n\n### Structure (all required sections present)\n- **Overview** — feature scope table, risk areas (form state machine, mobile drawer, responsive overflow, bundle size)\n- **Test Strategy** — Vitest + Playwright frameworks, browser matrix (Chromium P0, Firefox/WebKit P1, mobile Chromium P0), parallelisation config, 60/30/10 coverage split\n- **Authentication** — N/A for v1.0 with future storageState guidance\n- **Test Data** — inline fixtures, `vi.useFakeTimers()` guidance for async form tests, E2E form data, mock submit contract\n- **E2E Test Cases** — 49 test cases (TC-001 through TC-049)\n- **Acceptance Criteria** — pass/fail thresholds for unit, E2E, performance, and accessibility\n\n### Test Case Breakdown\n| Category | Framework | Count | Key Coverage |\n|----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\n| E2E | Playwright | 18 (TC-001–TC-018) | All 6 original E2E scenarios + responsive, multi-column, info block |\n| Unit | Vitest | 24 (TC-019–TC-049) | Every component + mock utility + theme tokens |\n| Integration | Vitest | 7 (TC-031, TC-032, TC-040, TC-041, TC-046–TC-049) | Navigation flows, full form lifecycle, theme propagation |\n\n### All User Stories Covered\n- **US-1** (Landing page): TC-001–003, TC-019, TC-024–026, TC-046–048\n- **US-2** (Navigation): TC-004–006, TC-028–032, TC-046–047\n- **US-3** (Contact form): TC-007–010, TC-035–044, TC-049\n- **US-4** (Company info): TC-011, TC-027\n- **US-5** (Responsive): TC-012–018, TC-016–017",
